## Commands — and what healthy looks like

An agent that has never run these cannot tell a broken toolchain from a broken
change. Both print red. So each row carries the output you get when things are
**fine**.

| Do this | Command | Healthy output |
|---|---|---|
| Install deps | `<command>` | `<what success prints>` |
| Run the tests | `<the cache-defeating form — e.g. go test ./... -count=1>` | `<e.g. ok <pkg> 0.4s, no "(cached)">` |
| Lint / format | `<command>` | `<...>` |
| Build | `<command>` | `<...>` |
| Run it locally | `<command>` | `<the line that means it is up>` |

**The test command above is the only one that counts as verification.** Reading
the source is not verification, and a cached result is not a result. See
`docs/STORY-CONTRACT.md`.

